# T33234 — Port — Auto MDI/MDI-X — tb470 IE520 stack — 2026-09-29 — UNSUPPORTED (skip)

Verdict: UNSUPPORTED on this platform — the case cannot be run on the tb470 IE520 stack, and no
bench change unblocks it.
- What the case needs: a FIXED copper (RJ45, 10/100/1000BASE-T) switchport on the DUT whose
  resolved MDI/MDI-X role (`current polarity mdi|mdix`) can be read and forced.
- What the bench lacks: the AT-IE520-28GSX has no fixed copper port at all — every one of its
  28 front ports is an SFP/SFP+ cage. The stack's partner-cabled ports (1.0.2, 1.0.9, 1.0.13,
  3.0.2, 4.0.2, 4.0.9) all hold copper SFPs (AT-SPTXa/SPTXc/SP10TM/SPTX/SP10T); a linked copper
  SFP reads `current polarity auto` forever (run 2, 08:56:54; by hand 08:39/08:42).
- Terrence's ruling (2026-09-29, queue I-5): UNSUPPORTED, not a defect — per the AW+ `polarity`
  usage note ("applies to copper 10/100/1000BASE-T switch ports; does not apply to fiber ports"),
  for MDI/MDI-X an SFP/SFP+ cage is a fibre port whatever module it holds. Scope: MDI/MDI-X only;
  a copper pluggable keeps its copper identity for speed/duplex/media in every other test.
- Exact change that would unblock it: none on this bench. Only a DUT with a fixed copper
  switchport (a different product) can run this case; no cable, SFP, outlet or destack helps.
Run 3 (this log) is the script-side proof: Test-cases d9a08dd strips the pluggable cases and
gates every TestCase on the DUT property `has_fixed_copper_port`; on tb470 the framework marked
all 14 cases unsupported before running any, sent no test command, and power-cycled nothing.
Run labelled: clean.

Operator: bench-runner subagent (device-testing-61 = sentinel, /test-mode shape A; Terrence
away). Queue row 5.

